ready: 1
kind: module
id: capture
name: Capture
summary: >-
  Turns what happens into stored experience without upkeep: raw captures from agents and the owner,
  ingestion of runtime transcripts into scrubbed events and episodes, imports, repository and
  document seeding, and import of stacks written by an earlier Kernle release. Runs in the daemon's
  ingestion worker and in the Kernle core.
runs_in:
  - sys.daemon
  - sys.python
  - sys.cli
owns:
  - raw captures (DATA-RAW)
  - transcript events (DATA-EVENT)
  - ingestion cursors
invariants:
  - Secrets are scrubbed before anything is stored.
  - Each position in a session record becomes at most one event.
  - Kernle never captures its own injected context or its own model sessions as experience.
  - Imported and seeded content is third-party unless the owner marks it as their own.
rationale: >-
  Capture reads the runtimes' own session records instead of relying on the agent to write
  everything down. The records are complete and survive a missed hook, so a missed hook only
  delays memory. Explicit calls such as raw and episode remain for what the agent chooses to note.


  Raw captures expire on a schedule because they are the least processed and most sensitive layer;
  the memories derived from them keep a link that shows the source expired.
